      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the smallest whole number \\( n \\) (where \\( n > 4 \\)) such that both \\( n \\) and \\( n^2 \\) are clock equivalents, meaning \\( n \\) and \\( n^2 \\) have the same remainder when divided by 12.\n\nLet's denote the remainder when \\( n \\) is divided by 12 as \\( r \\), and the remainder when \\( n^2 \\) is divided by 12 as \\( s \\). Therefore, we need \\( r \\equiv s \\pmod{12} \\).\n\nGiven that 4 hours is clock equivalent to its square (16 hours), this implies:\n\\[ 4 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{12}, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ 4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{12}. \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the smallest \\( n > 4 \\) such that \\( n \\equiv n^2 \\pmod{12} \\). We will check each number greater than 4:\n\n1. For \\( n = 5 \\):\n   \\[ 5^2 = 25, \\]\n   \\[ 25 \\div 12 = 2 \\text{ remainder } 1, \\]\n   so \\( 25 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{12} \\).\n   Therefore, \\( 5 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{12} \\), which means \\( n = 5 \\) is not a solution.\n\n2. For \\( n = 6 \\):\n   \\[ 6^2 = 36, \\]\n   \\[ 36 \\div 12 = 3 \\text{ remainder } 0, \\]\n   so \\( 36 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12} \\).\n   Therefore, \\( 6 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{12} \\), which means \\( n = 6 \\) is not a solution.\n\n3. For \\( n = 7 \\):\n   \\[ 7^2 = 49, \\]\n   \\[ 49 \\div 12 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 1, \\]\n   so \\( 49 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{12} \\).\n   Therefore, \\( 7 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{12} \\), which means \\( n = 7 \\) is not a solution.\n\n4. For \\( n = 8 \\):\n   \\[ 8^2 = 64, \\]\n   \\[ 64 \\div 12 = 5 \\text{ remainder } 4, \\]\n   so \\( 64 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{12} \\).\n   Therefore, \\( 8 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{12} \\), which means \\( n = 8 \\) is not a solution.\n\n5. For \\( n = 9 \\):\n   \\[ 9^2 = 81, \\]\n   \\[ 81 \\div 12 = 6 \\text{ remainder } 9, \\]\n   so \\( 81 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{12} \\).\n   Therefore, \\( 9 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{12} \\), which means \\( n = 9 \\) is a solution.\n\nThus, the least whole number of hours that is greater than 4 hours and is \"clock equivalent\" to its square number of hours is \\( \\boxed{9} \\).",
